  "method": "Single background thread, 16 established streams, 8 waves; each wave writes four 128 KiB pieces per stream and receives/verifies those same four pieces. Roomy 1 MiB sockets at both ends. Queued supplies 512 KiB before the drain. Fragmented supplies and drains each 128 KiB piece. Pressured supplies 512 KiB, with 128 KiB downstream capacity; drain/write progress alternates with 128 KiB consumer reads. Marker cells add one co-ready byte from a small established stream per wave. Counted builds require its write to be serviced first. Both arms verify all bytes, EOF and reverse data/FIN. Thread CPU spans native relay drains only. Wall rate covers producer, drains, consumer and byte checks. One warmup per arm/cell. Twelve randomized pairs per cell, six runs in each arm order. Cell order randomized in each block. Percentiles bootstrap matched pairs. Primary cell is queued/alone. No IP, VM, dispatch timing or concurrent producer/consumer. Both caps use one binary. Actual syscall counts were collected separately from timing with the same code, work and cap in an instrumented build.",
